The user can download each dataset from its respective link and open it with a text editor or spreadsheet software like Microsoft Excel, Google Sheets, or LibreOffice Calc to view the data. Each row represents an individual audit, and columns provide details such as the title of the audit, the type (Business Audit, Official Controls, Local Authority Audits), a brief description, and possibly other relevant information like the intended year of the audit.

